.TH CASTMIRROR-GUI 1 "2026-09-23" "CastMirror 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
castmirror-gui \- GTK 4 desktop front end for CastMirror
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B castmirror-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B castmirror-gui
is the GTK 4 + libadwaita desktop application for CastMirror. It has no command
line options; all state is persisted in
.I ~/.config/castmirror/config.json
and shared with
.BR castmirror (1).
.PP
The window is organised into four views:
.TP
.B Cast
LAN receiver list with model glyphs, a display or single-window selector, the
six quality preset cards, an inline bitrate slider, and the primary Cast action.
.TP
.B Live
Real-time status banner, FPS / bitrate / RTT / packet-loss sparklines, the
adaptive ladder rung indicator, and the Freeze display and Mute TV audio
controls.
.TP
.B Settings
Video bitrate ceiling, capture frame rate, Opus audio quality, host speaker
mute, target playout buffer delay, LAN subnet scan, appearance theme, and the
hardware and network self-test wizard.
.TP
.B Logs
Searchable log console with severity filters, clipboard copy and quick access to
the log folder.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_SOFTWARE_ENCODE=1
Force FFmpeg libx264 software encoding even where VAAPI hardware encoding is
available.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_X11=1
Force X11 capture instead of the Wayland xdg-desktop-portal ScreenCast path.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/dir
Redirect the configuration directory, as for
.BR castmirror (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/config.json
Persisted settings, shared with the CLI.
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror.log
Rotating debug log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR castmirror (1),
.BR xdg-desktop-portal (1),
.BR pipewire (1)
.SH NOTES
On Wayland the desktop portal asks which screen or window to share when a
session starts. System tray integration requires the Ayatana AppIndicator
library at build time; without it the application still runs and simply has no
tray icon.
.PP
Distributing a compiled CastMirror binary linked against GPL-licensed libx264
generally requires treating that binary as GPL. See the NOTICE file shipped
with the source.
